<h2 id="sec-2">Selection Criteria</h2>
<p>Our evaluation focused on five critical factors that directly impact your work experience and eye comfort:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Color Temperature Range:</strong> Can it produce both warm (2700K) and cool (5000K+) light for different tasks and times of day?</li>
<li><strong>Brightness Levels:</strong> Minimum 300 lumens for task lighting, with multiple brightness steps</li>
<li><strong>Eye Comfort Features:</strong> Flicker-free technology, blue light reduction, uniform light distribution</li>
<li><strong>Adjustability:</strong> Arm reach, head tilt range, and base stability</li>
<li><strong>Build Quality & Design:</strong> Materials, finish, footprint, and aesthetic compatibility with home offices</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="sec-3">In-Depth Reviews</h2>

<h3>1. BenQ ScreenBar Halo — Best Overall</h3>
<p>The BenQ ScreenBar Halo is the gold standard for monitor-mounted desk lamps. Its asymmetric optical design directs light precisely onto your workspace while keeping your screen glare-free — a breakthrough that eliminates the shadow-and-glare problems of traditional desk lamps.</p>
<p>The wireless magnetic controller is a thoughtful touch, allowing you to adjust brightness and color temperature without reaching for the lamp. Auto-dimming based on ambient light ensures optimal brightness throughout the day. At 109.95, it's a premium investment that pays for itself in reduced eye strain during long work sessions.</p>
