<h3>2. Xiaomi Mi Desk Lamp 2 — Best Value</h3>
<p>At under $35, the Xiaomi Mi Desk Lamp 2 punches far above its price point. The app-controlled auto-dimming feature learns your environment and adjusts accordingly, while the touch-sensitive arm allows intuitive brightness and color temperature adjustments. The sleek, minimalist design complements any modern workspace.</p>
<p>With 12 levelsof brightness and 4 color temperature settings (2700K-6500K), it covers every lighting need from late-night reading to bright morning focus work.</p>

<h3>3. TaoTronics LED Desk Lamp — Best Touch Controls</h3>
<p>The TaoTronics LED Desk Lamp excels in user experience with its intuitive touch panel. Five preset color modes (Reading, Focus, Relax, Rest, Custom) make it effortless to set the right atmosphere for any task. The 52-LED array provides uniform, flicker-free illumination across a 20-inch workspace.</p>
<p>The foldable arm design makes it compact for storage, and the built-in USB charging port is a welcome addition for keeping your devices powered.</p>

<h2 id="sec-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>What is the best color temperature for working from home?</h3>
<p>For focused work during the day, 4000K-5000K (cool white to daylight) is ideal as it promotes alertness. For evening work or relaxation, 2700K-3000K (warm white) is better to avoid disrupting your circadian rhythm. Lamps with adjustable color temperature, like the BenQ ScreenBar Halo, offer the most flexibility.</p>

<h3>Are LED desk lamps better for eye strain?</h3>
<p>Yes, when chosen correctly. Look for lamps labeled "flicker-free" and "blue light reduced." LEDs produce very little UV radiation and can be engineered to minimize harsh blue light peaks. The BenQ ScreenBar Halo and TaoTronics models both meet these criteria.</p>

<h3>Should I get a clip-on or free-standing desk lamp?</h3>
<p>Clip-on lamps save desk space and are ideal for small workstations, while free-standing lamps offer greater stability and usually more adjustable arms. For most home offices, a free-standing lamp with a weighted base provides the best combination of adjustability and stability.</p>

<h3>How many lumens do I need for a desk lamp?</h3>
<p>For task lighting at a desk, aim for 400-800 lumens. This provides sufficient brightness for reading, writing, and screen work without causing glare. Our top picks all fall within this range.</p>

